(PHARMACEUTICAL DEVIATION INVESTIGATION REPORT) Tj
T* (Document ID: DEV-2026-0881) Tj
T* (Site: Vertex API Manufacturing Facility 2) Tj
T* (Date: 2026-10-22) Tj
T* (Batch Number: BZ-2026-881) Tj
T* (Product: Benztropine Mesylate API) Tj
T* (Process Step: Vacuum Tray Drying \(Dryer VTD-03\)) Tj
T* (Severity: Major) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (DEVIATION DESCRIPTION:) Tj
T* (During final quality release testing, Batch BZ-2026-881 exhibited residual Acetone of 0.72% w/w by gas chromatography, exceeding the finished API acceptance specification of <= 0.50% w/w. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (PROCESS OBSERVATIONS:) Tj
T* (Drying was scheduled for 16 hours at 45C under 15 mbar vacuum in Dryer VTD-03. At hour 09:15, cooling water recirculator valve CV-102 failed closed, causing condenser cooling water temperature to spike to 28C against the maximum limit of 10C for 3.5 hours. Lower trays retained significant moisture and residual solvent.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (POTENTIAL CONTRIBUTING FACTORS:) Tj
T* (1. Equipment: Chilled water valve CV-102 actuator diaphragm fatigue.) Tj
T* (2. Method: Absence of automatic audible interlock when condenser temperature exceeds 15C.) Tj
T* (3. Measurement: Thermocouple TT-09 on lower shelf showed sluggish response during temperature ramp.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (RECOMMENDED IMMEDIATE ACTION:) Tj
T* (Quarantine Batch BZ-2026-881 in warehouse secure holding area.) Tj
ET
